---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Play online
description: "Where to play Canadian Highlander online: weekly Discord tournaments, monthly leagues on webcam, Cockatrice and MTGO, and pickup games."
pageClass: play
permalink: /play/
---
<header class="page-head page-head--play">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Play</p>
    <h1 class="page-head__title">Play Canlander online</h1>
    <p class="page-head__lede">Most of the action happens in the Canadian Highlander Discord. It has over {{ play.discordMembers }} members, a tournament every Saturday and Sunday, monthly leagues, and people looking for games at most hours. It's free to join and free to play.</p>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--brass" href="{{ site.discord }}">Join the Discord</a>
      <a class="link-arrow" href="#weeklies">See the schedule <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section section--tight" id="weeklies">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Weekly tournaments</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Every Saturday and Sunday</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__lede">Both weeklies are three rounds of Swiss, fifty minutes a round, then a final. You don't submit a decklist, so you can show up with whatever you feel like playing that day.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="board">
      {%- for e in play.weeklies %}
      <article class="board__event" data-weekly data-day="{{ e.dayIndex }}" data-hour="{{ e.hour }}">
        <header class="board__top">
          <span class="board__day">{{ e.day }}</span>
          <span class="board__platform mono">{{ e.platform }}</span>
        </header>
        <p class="board__time"><span class="board__clock">10:00</span><span class="board__ampm">am Pacific</span></p>
        <p class="board__local mono" data-local>&nbsp;</p>
        <h3 class="board__name">{{ e.name }}</h3>
        <p class="board__blurb">{{ e.blurb }}</p>
        <dl class="board__facts">
          <div><dt>Rounds</dt><dd>3 + final</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Round clock</dt><dd>50 min</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Decklist</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <ol class="howto">
      <li><span class="howto__n mono">01</span><div><h3>Join the Discord</h3><p>Sign-ups, pairings and the full event rules are all posted in the tournament channels on the <a href="{{ site.discord }}">Discord</a>.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="howto__n mono">02</span><div><h3>Get set up</h3><p>For webcam, you need a camera pointed at your play area. For Cockatrice, install the client and load your list before the start time.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="howto__n mono">03</span><div><h3>Play your rounds</h3><p>Message your opponent, play your match and report the result. Keep an eye on the clock, fifty minutes goes quickly.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="howto__n mono">04</span><div><h3>Top of the table</h3><p>The best records after three rounds play the final. Good finishes through the year can get you invited to the year-end invitational.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--felt" id="leagues">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Monthly leagues</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Can't make the weekend?</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__lede">There are three async leagues each month. You get your pairings, sort out a time with your opponent, and play before the round closes. The top eight play off at the end of the month.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="leagues">
      {%- for l in play.leagues %}
      <article class="league">
        <p class="league__platform mono">{{ l.platform }}</p>
        <h3 class="league__name">{{ l.name }}</h3>
        <p class="league__format">{{ l.format }}</p>
        <p class="league__lists"><span class="mono">Decklists</span> {{ l.lists }}</p>
        <p class="league__note">{{ l.note }}</p>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="glossnote"><b>Locked</b> means you play the same list all month. <b>Open</b> lists are public, <b>closed</b> lists are only seen by the organizers.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="pickup">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split__aside">
      <p class="eyebrow">Pickup games</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Just want a game?</h2>
      <p>Post in the looking-for-game channel and say how you want to play (webcam, Cockatrice or MTGO). There's usually someone around. If it's your first time, mention it. People are happy to slow down and explain what their cards do.</p>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ site.discord }}">Find a match ↗</a>
    </div>
    <div class="lfg" aria-label="What to post when looking for a game">
      <p class="lfg__label mono">A good looking-for-game post</p>
      <p class="lfg__post"><span class="lfg__tag">LFG</span> Webcam · Boros Aggro · new to the format, happy to go slow</p>
      <ul class="lfg__parts">
        <li><b>How</b> webcam, Cockatrice or MTGO</li>
        <li><b>What</b> the deck you're bringing</li>
        <li><b>Who</b> first game, casual, or testing for the weekly</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--rule" id="tables">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Clients</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Ways to play online</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tables">
      {%- for t in play.clients %}
      <a class="tablecard" href="{{ t.url }}">
        <span class="tablecard__kind mono">{{ t.kind }}</span>
        <span class="tablecard__name">{{ t.name }}</span>
        <span class="tablecard__desc">{{ t.desc }}</span>
        <span class="tablecard__cost mono">{{ t.cost }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--rule" id="proxies">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split__aside">
      <p class="eyebrow">Proxies</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Proxy friendly</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The Discord's webcam tournaments allow proxies. They need to show the card's full Oracle text and can't look like a real card. A printout sleeved in front of a basic land works fine.</p>
      <p>In paper it depends on the store. Yellowjacket Comics in Victoria, where the format started, allows ten proxies per deck, and a lot of stores allow more. Check before the event.</p>
      <p>Looking for paper games near you? There's a <a href="{{ site.official.home }}">list of regular events</a> linked from the official site, and the Discord has regional channels.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section cta-band">
  <div class="wrap cta-band__inner">
    <h2 class="h2">The next weekly is Saturday at 10 am Pacific</h2>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--brass" href="{{ site.discord }}">Join the Discord</a>
      <a class="link-arrow" href="/decks/">Need a deck? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
